  "stage_ignores": [
    {"what":"state.alive","at":"rise_from_zero","why":"DIVERGENCE F480: B5 (engine.js `_deathPending`, in test_stage_mirror.py KNOWN_UNMIRRORED): the engine holds a stale zero-HP echo for a short settle window after a revive; the stage books any zero as a death at once, so `alive` differs here."},
    {"what":"checkpoint:stale_zero_held:writes","why":"DIVERGENCE F479: the revive burst differs. The engine writes the `$SIR` hit-table rows (and, on a kill, the `$IRTX` S57 callouts) in the revive write, in a fixed order after the spawn line. The stage's `revive()` arms the table later (`_arm_life`) and sends no callouts, so the writes land at other checkpoints. The harness presses the stage's revive at the engine's `respawn.delay_s` (the stage has no auto-respawn timer)."},
    {"what":"state.alive","at":"stale_zero_held","why":"DIVERGENCE F480: B5 (engine.js `_deathPending`, in test_stage_mirror.py KNOWN_UNMIRRORED): the engine holds a stale zero-HP echo for a short settle window after a revive; the stage books any zero as a death at once, so `alive` differs here."},
    {"what":"checkpoint:revived_again:writes","why":"DIVERGENCE F479: the revive burst differs. The engine writes the `$SIR` hit-table rows (and, on a kill, the `$IRTX` S57 callouts) in the revive write, in a fixed order after the spawn line. The stage's `revive()` arms the table later (`_arm_life`) and sends no callouts, so the writes land at other checkpoints. The harness presses the stage's revive at the engine's `respawn.delay_s` (the stage has no auto-respawn timer)."},
    {"what":"checkpoint:armed_zero_is_death:writes","why":"DIVERGENCE F479: the revive burst differs. The engine writes the `$SIR` hit-table rows (and, on a kill, the `$IRTX` S57 callouts) in the revive write, in a fixed order after the spawn line. The stage's `revive()` arms the table later (`_arm_life`) and sends no callouts, so the writes land at other checkpoints. The harness presses the stage's revive at the engine's `respawn.delay_s` (the stage has no auto-respawn timer)."},
    {"what":"checkpoint:revived:writes","why":"DIVERGENCE F479: the revive burst differs. The engine writes the `$SIR` hit-table rows (and, on a kill, the `$IRTX` S57 callouts) in the revive write, in a fixed order after the spawn line. The stage's `revive()` arms the table later (`_arm_life`) and sends no callouts, so the writes land at other checkpoints. The harness presses the stage's revive at the engine's `respawn.delay_s` (the stage has no auto-respawn timer)."},
    {"what":"state.moment","why":"The stage has no HUD moment slot to expose as state (its `_moment` is an internal gate); the HUD reads the engine's."},
    {"what":"state.deaths","why":"The stage keeps no death count (MC and the HUD read the engine's); `alive` is compared instead."},
    {"what":"state.phase","why":"The stage has no MC link, so it has no match phase; it is armed and spawned by its own buttons."}
  ],
